  "answer":"When a search (or any tool) times out, the system must either abstain from answering or ask the user for clarification, and it must never rely on invalid evidence. A drift alert by itself is not sufficient to promote a new model to production; drift only triggers training of a challenger and its evaluation, and any production change still requires the standard hold‑out evaluation criteria before promotion.",
